    "created_at": "2018-02-14T23:18:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-14T23:18:14Z",
    "body": "Edge does (0, 0) in all cases. Haven't tested Safari.\r\n\r\nSo by my reading Chrome resets to the end for both reset() and the value setter, whereas Firefox follows the letter of the spec and resets to the end when the value setter is invoked but doesn't move the cursor when the form is reset.\r\n\r\nOf course, if we had `value=\"\"`, you'd have to move the cursor anyway, so it seems more like a spec omission...\r\n\r\nI guess this is just another bug in the vein of https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2424 and https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2411. In particular, see https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2424#issuecomment-286580627",
